<Quota name="Q-PerAppDay" type="calendar">
  <DisplayName>Tier 1: whole use case (calling app), per day</DisplayName>
  <!--
    Outer tier of quota(use case) x quota(department within it, see
    Q-PerDepartmentPerDay) x quota(user within that department, see
    Q-PerUserPerMinute). Identified by client_id alone: each of Translation,
    Sales-Agent and NaaS holds its own developer app on aicoe-llm, so this
    partitions automatically — no path condition needed the way
    aihub-api-v1's equivalent tier does, because this proxy's callers are
    genuinely distinct credentials, not one shared app on different paths.

    Reads a developer-app attribute, not a product attribute — same pattern
    PTL-PromptTokenLimit already uses — so each app's own ceiling can be
    tuned independently in the console without touching this file or the
    shared aicoe-llm product. The literal fallback is a provisional default,
    not measured traffic; size it against real usage before trusting it. See
    BUILD-LOG.md.

    Deliberately does NOT touch the token budget (LTQ-Enforce/LTQ-Count) —
    see AM-Identity.xml's comment on llm_dept_app_user for why that pair
    stays keyed on department alone for now.
  -->
  <StartTime>2026-01-01 00:00:00</StartTime>
  <Interval>1</Interval>
  <TimeUnit>day</TimeUnit>
  <Allow count="50000" countRef="verifyapikey.VA-ApiKey.developer.app.attribute.req_per_day_app"/>
  <Identifier ref="verifyapikey.VA-ApiKey.client_id"/>
  <Distributed>true</Distributed>
  <Synchronous>true</Synchronous>
</Quota>
